uly 29 at 2:31PM MDT until July 29 at 5:30PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"FFWPUB\n\nThe National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nSoutheastern Teller County in central Colorado...\n\n* Until 530 PM MDT.\n\n* At 231 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 1 and 2 inches of rain\nhave fallen. The expected rainfall rate is 1 to 2 inches in 1 hour.\nAdditional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1.5 inches are possible in\nthe warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, rural roads\nand normally dry washes, as well as other poor drainage\nand low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nVictor.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nWest Beaver Creek, Middle Beaver Creek, Wilson Creek and their\ntributaries.","ends":"2026-07-29T17:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Teller, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.78e697ea6466628b922f667697a9d89522f13e53.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.78e697ea6466628b922f667697a9d89522f13e53.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-07-29T18:28:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 291828 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1228 PM MDT Wed Jul 29 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - One more day of organized heavy rain activity, flash flooding likely over parts of the region. - Drier THU/FRI/SAT, then hot SUN, MON - Rain chances increase and possibly cooler stating TUE && .SHORT TERM /THROUGH THURSDAY/... Issued at 1227 PM MDT Wed Jul 29 202","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-07-29T17:06:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 291706 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook Nationa